{"from": "claim:jn-18-01-kidron-garden", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-36-gethsemane", "note": "Matthew names the place Gethsemane and sets it on the Mount of Olives; John says only 'a garden' across the Kidron - the same Passion-night venue told with different topographical details."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-01-kidron-garden", "type": "related_to", "to": "place:gethsemane", "note": "John never names Gethsemane; 'the garden' across the Kidron is traditionally identified with it."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-03-arrest-party", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-47-armed-crowd", "note": "Matthew has a great crowd with swords and clubs sent from the chief priests and elders; John has a Roman detachment (speira) plus officers from the chief priests and Pharisees - different composition of the arresting force."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-10-malchus", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-51-sword-ear", "note": "Matthew leaves the high priest's servant unnamed and does not say which ear; John names Malchus and specifies the right ear (Luke adds that Jesus healed it)."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-13-annas-first", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-57-led-to-caiaphas", "note": "Matthew and Mark bring Jesus straight to Caiaphas the high priest; John interposes an initial hearing before Annas, then Annas sends him bound to Caiaphas."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-15-other-disciple", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-58-peters-in-courtyard", "note": "Matthew has Peter simply follow at a distance into the court; John alone tells how an unnamed disciple known to the high priest brought Peter past the doorkeeper."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-17-denials", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-34-cockcrow-denial", "note": "John's three denials in the high priest's courtyard and the cockcrow answer the prediction Matthew and Mark record; John, like Luke, records a single crow after the third denial."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-17-denials", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-14-30-cockcrow-twice", "note": "Mark specifies a second cockcrow within the night ('before the rooster crows twice'); John records only that the rooster crowed after the third denial - no 'twice'."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-28-defilement", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-17-prepare-passover", "note": "John's chronology: on the day of the trial the leaders still intend to eat the Passover that evening, so the meal falls after the crucifixion; in the Synoptics the Passover meal was eaten the night before (the Last Supper)."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-28-defilement", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-14-12-sacrificed-passover", "note": "Mark's 'when they sacrificed the Passover' puts the lamb slaughter and meal on the day before the crucifixion; John has the leaders not yet eaten the Passover on the crucifixion day - the two chronologies differ by a day."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-33-king-question", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-11-14-jesus-before-governor", "note": "The same hearing before Pilate; Matthew reports the governor's question and Jesus's brief 'You say so' with the silent response to charges, John preserves the extended dialogue about kingship."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-33-king-question", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-23-02-charges", "note": "Luke's leaders spell out the political charges (perverting the nation, forbidding tribute, claiming to be king); John's leaders say only 'evildoer', and the 'King of the Jews' issue emerges in Pilate's questioning."}
{"from": "claim:jn-18-40-barabbas-robber", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-15-07-barabbas-insurgents", "note": "Mark binds Barabbas with insurgents who had committed murder in the insurrection; John characterizes him only as a robber (lestes) - different descriptions of the same man."}
